preloader-stock.img is not part of this package.

The stock SPI preloader is Miyoo vendor firmware: DDR init and the SPL, 2 MiB.
The script and checker in this package are MIT. That license does not cover
the vendor image, and this package does not install it.

Origin recorded by the hardware wiki, not a file shipped here:
  Zetarancio/Miyoo-Flip-Mainline-Linux-Reverse-Engineering
  commit c126d3235face9ddca5bf021258a84758dca543c
  preloader-stock-rocknix/App/apommel-multiboot/preloader-stock.img
  introducing commit 8ef495f5711ce13645e9c68df63b7d7a9934cf7e
  SHA-256 dfdd7d20d6fd3beb18350dcf8fa58740b40b4baaf39467d45076f949053a2922
  historical MD5 1d525e6e6c89bd788b5245c90c97833b

The wiki says those bytes match the first 2 MiB of spi_20241119160817.img.
It also says more than one stock SPL build exists. The known patched
counterpart, fingerprint only, is preloader-patched.img, SHA-256
ed10591f62ae0b8845ac9bd6cf80c896a2b172d32c7c4ef6564d305e8662c13d.

Redistribution remains unspecified. The wiki records where the bytes came
from. It does not contain a license, a copyright grant, or permission from
Miyoo to redistribute this preloader. A sentence about a shared DRAM blob
matching public rkbin is not a license for the image.

Zlyme therefore does not ship the file and does not use it as a restore
fallback. Restore stock writes only this unit's /boot/mtd5-original-<sha256>.img.
If that backup is absent, stock restore is unavailable. Arm and disarm do
not need it.
